# Android — keep the project, ignore local/generated artifacts only
android/local.properties
android/**/build/
android/.gradle/
android/.kotlin/
android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
android/captures/
android/gradlew.log
# android/key.properties and the release keystore ARE committed
# deliberately — see android/key.properties. This environment is
# ephemeral and has no persistent storage outside the git repo, so a
# gitignored keystore/debug key gets silently regenerated on every
# reset, invalidating every SHA fingerprint registered in Firebase
# Console and breaking phone-auth SMS delivery across all three apps.
# Committing a fixed release keystore is the tradeoff that keeps
# signing (and Firebase Phone Auth) stable across resets.

